  "details": "<p><em>The Barrington Atlas Directory</em> notes: Fioccaglia di Flumeri. Archaeological excavations in the 1980s (1986, 1989) explored portions of at least one\u00a0<em>domus\u00a0</em>at the site. Non-invasive geophysical prospection and UAV survey in 2025 revealed additional subsurface features, including a likely forum area, a possible theater, and additional\u00a0<em>domus</em>.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "Fioccaglia di Flumeri was the site of a Gracchan colony. Some scholars identify the archaeological site at Fioccaglia di Flumeri with the ancient Forum Aemilii.",
